<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trenggana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1546">1546</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Trenggana, Sultan Trenggana of Demak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trenggana was sultan of Demak in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> from about 1521 to 1546, under whom the sultanate reached its greatest extent, conquering much of eastern Java and taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-kelapa">Sunda Kelapa</a>. He was killed during a campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panarukan">Panarukan</a> in 1546, and the succession war that followed broke up Demak and led to the rise of Pajang.</p></div>
